{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-34738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-34738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 22 & 22 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{3}{22}{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 22 & 22 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ 22{x}_{2}=22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-{x}_{1}+4(1)=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-2+1=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-34738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1cba08bde9be8a67f716bb10d15f894d4ec97f0a080997a2b28261be86606266"} {"question" "q-34738" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-34738" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "x\\notin \\text{span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-34738" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-34764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-34764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ -{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ 0=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the fourth equation is always false. Therefore, the system has no solution and we conclude that \n\n$$\nx\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-34764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1cba08bde9be8a67f716bb10d15f894d4ec97f0a080997a2b28261be86606266"} {"question" "q-34764" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-34764" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-34764" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-35218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-35218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -8 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -8 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n4{x}_{1}+3\\cdot 2=10\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=1+2=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-35218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1cba08bde9be8a67f716bb10d15f894d4ec97f0a080997a2b28261be86606266"} {"question" "q-35218" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-35218" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "x\\notin \\text{span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-35218" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-75978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-75978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,-8\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,4\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}+{{(\\,2\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{3}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=-8\\cdot {b}_{1}+4\\cdot {b}_{2}+2\\cdot {b}_{3}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{2}=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-75978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1cba08bde9be8a67f716bb10d15f894d4ec97f0a080997a2b28261be86606266"} {"question" "q-75978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-75978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-8"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-75978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-112203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072390/state.json" "file_sha256" "06a6682c101f40c3d398dd5320712df04e74859a4deffb74df78dc7938dbc70b"} {"question" "q-112203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,8\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=3\\cdot {b}_{1}+8\\cdot {b}_{2}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that ${x}_{1}=3